BANKWISE DEMO BANK
KYC GUIDELINES

1. INTRODUCTION

KYC stands for Know Your Customer. KYC is a customer verification process used by banks and financial institutions to establish and maintain customer identity information.

KYC helps financial institutions understand who their customers are and supports the prevention of financial fraud and misuse of banking services.

This is a fictional/demo document created for the BankWise AI RAG project. It is not an official banking policy.

2. PURPOSE OF KYC

The main purposes of KYC include:

• Verifying customer identity
• Maintaining accurate customer information
• Supporting secure banking services
• Reducing identity-related fraud
• Supporting applicable financial regulations

3. COMMON KYC INFORMATION

Depending on the account and applicable requirements, customers may be asked to provide information such as:

• Full name
• Date of birth
• Residential address
• Mobile number
• Email address
• Identity information
• Other information required by the bank

The exact requirements depend on the bank and applicable regulations.

4. KYC DOCUMENTS

A bank may request documents to verify identity and address.

Examples may include:

• Government-approved identity documents
• Address proof
• Photograph, where applicable
• Other documents specified by the bank

Customers should provide documents only through verified official banking channels.

5. KYC DURING ACCOUNT OPENING

KYC verification is generally part of the account-opening process.

A customer may need to:

• Provide the requested information.
• Submit required documents.
• Complete the bank's verification process.
• Provide additional information if requested.
• Wait for the bank to complete verification.

The exact process may differ depending on the account type and bank.

6. KYC UPDATE

Customers may need to update their KYC information when requested by the bank or when their information changes.

Examples include:

• Change of address
• Change in contact information
• Changes to other customer information
• Periodic verification requested by the bank

Customers should use official banking channels for KYC updates.

7. ONLINE KYC

Some banks may provide digital or online KYC facilities.

Customers should access online KYC services only through:

• The bank's official website
• The bank's official mobile application
• Other verified channels provided by the bank

Customers should avoid links received from unknown sources.

8. KYC VERIFICATION PROCESS

A general KYC process may include:

Step 1: Customer provides the requested information.

Step 2: Customer submits the required documents.

Step 3: The bank verifies the submitted information.

Step 4: Additional information may be requested if necessary.

Step 5: The bank completes the verification according to its procedures.

The actual process can vary between banks.

9. KYC AND MOBILE NUMBER

A bank may associate a verified mobile number with a customer's account.

Customers should keep their contact information updated through official banking channels.

10. KYC AND ADDRESS CHANGE

If a customer changes their residential address, they should follow the bank's official process for updating address information.

The bank may request appropriate supporting documentation.

11. KYC DOCUMENT SECURITY

Customers should protect copies of their identity and address documents.

Important safety practices include:

• Do not send documents to unknown people.
• Do not upload documents to suspicious websites.
• Verify the bank's website before submitting documents.
• Avoid sharing unnecessary personal information.
• Use official banking applications and websites.

12. KYC FRAUD AWARENESS

Fraudsters may impersonate bank employees and request KYC information.

Customers should be careful if someone asks for:

• OTP
• ATM PIN
• UPI PIN
• CVV
• Internet banking password
• Full card details
• Authentication codes

Customers should never disclose confidential authentication credentials.

13. SUSPICIOUS KYC REQUEST

If a customer receives a suspicious message or call claiming that their KYC will be blocked unless they provide sensitive information, they should not follow the instructions immediately.

Instead, the customer should contact the bank through an official website, application, helpline, or branch.

14. KYC FAILURE OR PENDING STATUS

If KYC verification is unsuccessful or remains pending, customers should check the status through an official bank channel.

The bank may request corrected or additional information.

Customers should follow the bank's official instructions.

15. KYC FOR EXISTING CUSTOMERS

Existing customers may occasionally be required to update or confirm their KYC information.

Customers should respond through the bank's official process and keep their information accurate.

16. IMPORTANCE OF ACCURATE INFORMATION

Customers should provide accurate information during KYC.

Incorrect or outdated information may cause difficulties with account services or verification.

17. BANKWISE AI LIMITATION

BankWise AI is an informational chatbot created for a demonstration RAG project.

It cannot:

• Perform real KYC verification
• Verify identity documents
• Access customer accounts
• Store customer identity documents
• Update real KYC information
• Approve or reject KYC
• Contact the bank on behalf of a customer

For real KYC-related issues, customers should contact their actual bank through an official channel.

DISCLAIMER

KYC requirements, accepted documents, verification methods, procedures, and regulatory requirements may vary between banks and may change over time.

This document provides general information for demonstration purposes only. Always verify current KYC requirements through the relevant bank's official channels.
